Ben: Yes! I watched ''My Crazy Family'' at the weekend. I laughed my head off.
Anna: Really? Was it that funny?
Ben: It was. There is one scene where the dad falls into a huge cake. I almost cried with laughter.
Anna: It sounds great. Who is in it?
Ben: A famous comedian called Tom Lee. His timing is perfect.
Anna: Then I must watch it tonight. Thanks for the tip!
Ben: Enjoy it. Just don''t drink anything while you watch, or you''ll spill it laughing!', 'Anna 问 Ben 最近有没有看好喜剧;Ben 周末看了《我的疯狂家庭》,笑得不行;有一幕爸爸掉进大蛋糕,他差点笑哭;主演是著名笑星 Tom Lee,节奏感极好;Anna 决定今晚就看;Ben 提醒她看时别喝东西,以免笑着洒出来。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What did Ben watch at the weekend?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["A comedy called ''My Crazy Family''.","A sad and serious film.","A long news programme.","A children''s cartoon."]},{"q":"How did Ben feel while watching it?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Bored and sleepy.","He laughed a great deal.","Rather frightened.","Angry and upset."]},{"q":"What happens in the scene Ben describes?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["The father falls into a cake.","A dog runs onto the stage.","The lights suddenly go out.","A car breaks down."]},{"q":"Who stars in the film?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["A famous singer.","A comedian named Tom Lee.","A football player.","A young teacher."]},{"q":"What does Ben warn Anna not to do?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Watch it too late at night.","Tell anyone the ending.","Drink while watching, or she''ll spill it laughing.","Sit too close to the screen."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective1', 'U1', 'fltrp');
They wear bright wigs and big red noses to make sick children smile.
On a normal day, they tell jokes, sing songs and do magic tricks.
They always work together with the real doctors and nurses.
Their goal is simple: to make a frightening place feel a little friendlier.', '小丑医生是受过专门训练、在医院工作的表演者;他们戴鲜艳假发和大红鼻子逗患病儿童笑;平常会讲笑话、唱歌、变魔术;总是和真正的医生护士一起工作;目标很简单:让令人害怕的地方变得友善一点。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Where do clown doctors work?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["In schools.","In shops.","In factories.","In hospitals."]},{"q":"What do clown doctors wear?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Bright wigs and big red noses.","Plain white coats only.","Football kits.","Long black robes."]},{"q":"What do they do on a normal day?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Clean the whole hospital.","Tell jokes, sing songs and do magic tricks.","Drive the ambulances.","Cook meals for everyone."]},{"q":"Who do clown doctors work with?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Only other clowns.","The hospital cleaners.","The real doctors and nurses.","Nobody at all."]},{"q":"What is their main goal?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["To earn as much money as possible.","To become famous on television.","To replace the doctors.","To make a scary place feel friendlier."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective1', 'U1', 'fltrp');
Dan: Yes! My brother told me that school was closed for the whole day.
Cara: And did you believe him?
Dan: I did at first. I was so happy that I went straight back to bed!
Cara: Oh no. What happened then?
Dan: Mum came in and asked why I wasn''t ready. I had to run all the way to school.
Cara: That''s a classic trick. Were you late?
Dan: Just by five minutes. My brother couldn''t stop laughing all evening.', 'Cara 问 Dan 愚人节有没有被骗;Dan 说哥哥骗他学校全天停课;他起初信了,高兴地回去睡觉;妈妈进来问他为何没准备,他只好一路跑去学校;只迟到五分钟;哥哥一整晚都笑个不停。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What did Dan''s brother tell him?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["That school was closed for the day.","That it was going to snow.","That he had won a prize.","That dinner was ready."]},{"q":"Did Dan believe the trick at first?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["No, not for a second.","Yes, he believed it.","He never heard it.","He was already at school."]},{"q":"What did Dan do after hearing the news?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["He told his teacher.","He started his homework.","He went back to bed.","He called Cara."]},{"q":"Why did Dan have to run?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["He was chasing the bus.","He wanted some exercise.","He was late for a film.","He had been fooled and was late for school."]},{"q":"How did Dan''s brother feel that evening?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["He kept laughing about the trick.","He felt very sorry.","He was bored and tired.","He was angry with Dan."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective1', 'U1', 'fltrp');
One day he went into a barber''s shop for a shave.
The barber, who did not know him, asked if he had a ticket for Twain''s lecture that night.
Twain said that he did not.
''Then you''ll have to stand,'' said the barber, ''every seat has been sold.''
''That''s just my luck,'' Twain replied. ''I always have to stand when that man lectures.''', '马克·吐温以机智著称;一天他去理发店刮胡子;不认识他的理发师问他有没有当晚吐温讲座的票;吐温说没有;理发师说那你只能站着,座位都卖光了;吐温回道:''真倒霉,那家伙演讲时我总得站着。''', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Why did Twain go into the shop?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["To buy a ticket.","For a shave.","To give a talk.","To meet a friend."]},{"q":"Did the barber recognise Twain?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Yes, at once.","He had met him before.","No, he did not know him.","He was Twain''s friend."]},{"q":"What did the barber ask Twain about?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["His name.","His haircut.","The price of a shave.","A ticket for the lecture."]},{"q":"What did the barber say about the seats?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["They had all been sold.","They were very cheap.","They were free that night.","Half of them were empty."]},{"q":"Why is Twain''s reply funny?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["He had lost his ticket.","He joked as if he were not the lecturer himself.","He could not afford a seat.","He disliked the barber."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective1', 'U1', 'fltrp');
Sam: How about telling funny stories about our first day at school?
Eva: I like that. Everyone can understand it.
Sam: We should also add a surprise ending to each story.
Eva: Good. And let''s practise our timing, so the jokes land well.
Sam: Agreed. Maybe I can use a few simple props, like a giant pair of glasses.
Eva: Perfect. If we make the audience laugh in the first minute, the rest will be easy.
Sam: Then let''s start writing the script tonight.', 'Eva 和 Sam 商量校园演出的喜剧节目;Sam 提议讲开学第一天的趣事,大家都能懂;还要给每个故事加个出人意料的结尾;Eva 说要练好节奏让笑点到位;Sam 想用些简单道具,比如一副巨大的眼镜;Eva 说只要头一分钟逗笑观众,后面就轻松了;两人决定今晚开始写脚本。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What are Eva and Sam planning?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["A history lesson.","A football match.","A comedy act for the school show.","A music concert."]},{"q":"What will their stories be about?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["A famous scientist.","A trip to the moon.","A cooking class.","Their first day at school."]},{"q":"What will they add to each story?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["A surprise ending.","A long list of names.","A sad ending.","A maths question."]},{"q":"Why do they want to practise their timing?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["To finish faster.","So that the jokes land well.","To save money.","To remember their names."]},{"q":"What prop does Sam suggest using?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["A real bicycle.","A box of books.","A giant pair of glasses.","A football."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective1', 'U1', 'fltrp');
Scientists say that laughter helps the body make chemicals that lower stress.
It also brings people closer together.
You do not need an expensive ticket or a famous comedian.
A silly joke with a friend is often enough.
So next time you feel worried, share a laugh; it really is one of the best kinds of medicine.', '一个让生活更快乐的小贴士:每天都笑一笑;科学家说笑能帮身体产生降低压力的化学物质;它还能拉近人与人的距离;你不需要昂贵的票或著名笑星;和朋友说个傻笑话往往就够了;所以下次烦恼时,一起笑一笑吧,它真是最好的良药之一。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What is the tip in this passage?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["To sleep all day.","To buy expensive tickets.","To avoid your friends.","To laugh every day."]},{"q":"What does laughter help the body do?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Make chemicals that lower stress.","Grow much taller.","Stop feeling hungry.","Run much faster."]},{"q":"What else does laughter do?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["It makes people tired.","It brings people closer together.","It costs a lot of money.","It keeps people apart."]},{"q":"What do you need in order to laugh, according to the passage?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["A famous comedian.","An expensive ticket.","Not much; even a silly joke with a friend.","A large theatre."]},{"q":"What is laughter compared to at the end?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["A waste of time.","A difficult exam.","A long journey.","One of the best kinds of medicine."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective1', 'U1', 'fltrp');

